; Phonemes in, a record of five cards out for each phoneme and pause: pc s wf pms send; the host puts the first six
; cards of row pc of the phoneme table beside it (kind inh mn cls9 liq vls; a pause is pc 0, whose row is kind 8),
; to make the segment's record of 11. A phoneme card is 10 x code + stress; -1 is a word boundary, -2 a comma, -3 a
; period, -4 a question mark, -5 an exclamation mark, -9 the end. A pause's record has its length in ms (300 for a comma, else 600) and whether it ends a sentence (send 1, or 2 for
; a question). A 50 ms pause comes first; a 150 ms pause comes last and ends the last sentence too (send 3). The
; segment after a pause or a boundary starts a word (wf 1). WH's row is W's.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            start   CLA   c50      03-05: the pause at the start
  04                    STO   pms
  05                    JMP   rec
  06            loop    INP   t        06-15: a phoneme: pc and s
  07                    CLA   t
  08                    TAC   ctl
  09                    SFT   01
  10                    STO   pc
  11                    SFT   10
  12                    STO   x
  13                    CLA   t
  14                    SUB   x
  15                    STO   s
  16            rec     OUT   pc       16-20: the record
  17                    OUT   s
  18                    OUT   wf
  19                    OUT   pms
  20                    OUT   snd
  21            nxt     CLA   snd      21-35: stop after the end pause; wf 1 after a pause, else 0
  22                    SUB   n3
  23                    TAC   go
  24                    HRS   00
  25            go      CLA   z
  26                    SUB   pms
  27                    TAC   one
  28                    CLA   z
  29                    JMP   setw
  30            one     CLA   00
  31            setw    STO   wf
  32                    CLA   z
  33                    STO   pms
  34                    STO   snd
  35                    JMP   loop
  36            ctl     CLA   z        36-83: -1, a boundary: the next phoneme starts a word
  37                    STO   pc
  38                    STO   s
  39                    CLA   t
  40                    ADD   00
  41                    TAC   pa
  42                    CLA   00
  43                    STO   wf
  44                    JMP   loop
  45            pa      ADD   00       60-100: -2 to -5 pauses, -9 the end pause
  46                    TAC   p3
  47                    CLA   c300
  48                    STO   pms
  49                    JMP   rec
  50            p3      CLA   c600
  51                    STO   pms
  52                    CLA   t
  53                    ADD   n3
  54                    TAC   p4
  55                    CLA   00
  56                    JMP   sn
  57            p4      ADD   00
  58                    TAC   p5
  59                    CLA   n2
  60                    JMP   sn
  61            p5      ADD   00
  62                    TAC   pend
  63                    CLA   00
  64                    JMP   sn
  65            pend    CLA   c150
  66                    STO   pms
  67                    CLA   n3
  68            sn      STO   snd
  69                    JMP   rec
  70            t       DATA  0
  71            pc      DATA  0
  72            s       DATA  0
  73            wf      DATA  0
  74            pms     DATA  0
  75            snd     DATA  0
  76            x       DATA  0
  77            z       DATA  0
  78            c50     DATA  50
  79            n3      DATA  3
  80            n2      DATA  2
  81            c300    DATA  300
  82            c600    DATA  600
  83            c150    DATA  150
